<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Interview Questions Metadata</title>
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        body {
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #f8f9fa;
        }
        .container {
            max-width: 800px;
            background: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        .content {
            display: none;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="mb-4">📚💡 <strong>Interview Questions Metadata</strong></h2>
        <p>
            I built <strong>Interview Questions Metadata</strong>, a full-stack application designed to render Markdown files efficiently.
            <br/>
            <a href="/v1/pages/admin/content-details/itr1">/v1/pages/admin/content-details/itr1</a>
        </p>

        <button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm mb-3" onclick="toggleContent()">Read More</button>

        <div class="content">
            <h4>✅ <strong>Tech Stack:</strong></h4>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> EJS (Embedded JavaScript Templates)</li>
                <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Express.js</li>
                <li><strong>Testing:</strong> Jest</li>
                <li><strong>Data Fetching:</strong> Axios</li>
            </ul>

            <h4>✅ <strong>Key Features:</strong></h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Renders Markdown (<code>.md</code>) files placed in a <strong>base folder</strong> or any of its subdirectories.</li>
                <li>Uses <strong>Express and EJS</strong> for a smooth rendering experience.</li>
                <li>Working on an <strong>API to expose stored references</strong>, making it a centralized place for my static file references.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function toggleContent() {
            const content = document.querySelector('.content');
            const button = document.querySelector('button');
            if (content.style.display === 'none' || content.style.display === '') {
                content.style.display = 'block';
                button.textContent = 'Read Less';
            } else {
                content.style.display = 'none';
                button.textContent = 'Read More';
            }
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
